Third-party software in the CLI
-------------------------------
The CLI depends on commander (MIT), zod (MIT) and yaml (ISC).

Third-party software in the HTML report
---------------------------------------
The HTML report is a single file that bundles third-party open-source
software. Every generated report embeds the complete list of bundled packages
with their license texts in a comment at the top of the file. The npm package
ships the same list as dist/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

Licensing check (2026-10-11): the report bundles 42 packages. All of them are
licensed under Apache-2.0, MIT, ISC or BSD-3-Clause, and these licenses allow
redistribution in a single-file report when the license notices are included.
None of the Apache-2.0 packages ships a NOTICE file that needs to be carried
over. Two packages vendor third-party material under another license; both
notices are embedded in every report and in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. The
bundled packages include:

- UI5 Web Components, UI5 Web Components for React and their charts, icons,
  localization and theming packages (Apache-2.0)
  - @ui5/webcomponents-base vendors Preact (MIT, Copyright (c) 2015-present
    Jason Miller)
  - @ui5/webcomponents-localization vendors Unicode CLDR locale data
    (Unicode License v3, Copyright (c) 1991-2024 Unicode, Inc.)
- SAP Theming Base Content, including the "72" font files (Apache-2.0)
- React, React DOM, React Router, TanStack Query and TanStack Virtual (MIT)
- Recharts and its dependencies (MIT); D3 modules and internmap (ISC);
  victory-vendor (MIT AND ISC)
- lit-html (BSD-3-Clause)
